<header><p class="st-kicker">prince bishopric · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Prince-Archbishopric of Salzburg</h1><p class="st-meta">1213 CE – 1803 CE (approx.) · capital Salzburg</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Alpine church state that grew rich on salt and gold, built a baroque capital, expelled its Protestants in 1731 and employed the young Mozart.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rupert-of-salzburg">Saint Rupert</a> founded a church and monastery at the Roman town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iuvavum">Iuvavum</a> around 696, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a> became an archbishopric in 798. Its archbishops gained lands and immunities over the centuries, and by the early 13th century, around 1213, they were recognised as princes ruling a territory largely independent of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-bavaria">Duchy of Bavaria</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The archbishop, elected by the cathedral chapter, governed a land whose wealth came from salt at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hallein">Hallein</a> and gold and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> mines in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gastein-valley">Gastein</a> valley. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolf-dietrich-von-raitenau">Wolf Dietrich von Raitenau</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/markus-sittikus-von-hohenems">Markus Sittikus</a> rebuilt <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salzburg">Salzburg</a> in Italian baroque style, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris-lodron">Paris Lodron</a> kept it out of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-years-war">Thirty Years War</a>. In 1731 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leopold-anton-von-firmian">Leopold Anton von Firmian</a> expelled about 20,000 Protestants. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolfgang-amadeus-mozart">Mozart</a> was born there in 1756 and served Archbishop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hieronymus-von-colloredo">Hieronymus von Colloredo</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The see was secularised in 1803 as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/electorate-of-salzburg">Electorate of Salzburg</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ferdinand-iii-grand-duke-of-tuscany">Ferdinand of Tuscany</a>, then passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> in 1805 and to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a> in 1810. In 1816 most of it was returned to Austria, of which it is now a federal state.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/prince-archbishopric-of-salzburg.jpg" alt="Prince-Archbishopric of Salzburg" width="320" height="288"><figcaption>Image: Roke (map), Hanno Sandvik (addition of colours, based on Putzger Historischer Weltatlas, 103rd ed., 2005) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HRR_1648_Salzburg.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1213 CE – 1803 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>prince bishopric</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>theocratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Salzburg</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Wolf Dietrich von Raitenau, Paris Lodron, Hieronymus von Colloredo</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bavarian German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/austria">Austria</a>, <a href="/countries/germany">Germany</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Erzstift Salzburg, Archbishopric of Salzburg</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1508&amp;focus=prince-archbishopric-of-salzburg" aria-label="Prince-Archbishopric of Salzburg on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4984 503 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Prince-Archbishopric of Salzburg lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5304 759L5229 694M5304 759L5304 759"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5229 694h0M5304 759h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5304 759h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5304 759h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>